The later 2dbfe9001fa8e8b979ff80a1c88b888d48e1b575 rewrite cites readability
and x86-64 performance; no claim is made that this new adaptation has
received upstream review, audit, security certification or acceptance.
Original Go BSD copyright and license notices remain in the copied file.

The historical file is unchanged except five identifier renames and a
MIPSLE/gc/non-purego build constraint. Its key initialization, streaming,
reduction, carry and finalization bodies are not redesigned or converted.
The current 64-bit generic implementation remains as a test reference.
The sole current public-file change replaces New's initialization call
with an internal constructor hook. Other architectures and purego use the
original initialize function; only MIPSLE gc/non-purego selects the old
independent state. Public MAC methods and AEAD, Verify/finalized, ChaCha,
overlap and counter safety behavior are unchanged. No assembly is added.
This patch and its overlay are isolated from 003 and default builds.

